-- title:
--   Lemma 7.1 — reachability values equal limit-average values of $G_T$
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a concurrent stochastic game with transition function $\delta$ and let $T\subseteq S$ be a target set. Let $G_T$ be the game in which every target state is made absorbing,
--   $$\delta_T(s,a,b)=\begin{cases}\mathbf 1[s]&s\in T,\\ \delta(s,a,b)&\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\qquad r_T(s,a,b)=\begin{cases}1&s\in T,\\0&\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}$$
--   Then for every state $s$,
--   $$\mathrm{val}^G_T(s)=\mathrm{val}^{G_T}(s),$$
--   where the right-hand side is the value of $\mathrm{LimAvg}(r_T)$ in $G_T$. Moreover, if every target state is absorbing in $G$ (that is, $\delta(s,a,b)(s)=1$ for all $s\in T$ and all actions), then $G_T=G$.
--
--   This reduces reachability objectives to limit-average objectives with the same values, so the complexity results for limit-average objectives transfer to reachability. It covers $T=\emptyset$, $T=S$ and initial states in $T$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite game G = (S, A, B, δ) with |S| = n and at most m actions per player → states Fin n, actions Fin mA and Fin mB with n, mA, mB ≥ 1, m = max(mA, mB), distributions as nonnegative real vectors summing to one; reason: relabelling of finite sets; nonempty state and action sets are the source game convention
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Lemma 7.1, printed p. 30 (PDF p. 32)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Lemma 7.1 (Reachability as limit-average).** For a game `G` and target set `T`, let `G_T`
make every target state absorbing and let `r_T(s,a,b) = 1` for `s ∈ T` and `0` otherwise. Then
`val^G_T(s) = val^{G_T}(s)` (the value of `LimAvg(r_T)` in `G_T`) for all states `s`; and if every
target state is absorbing in `G`, then `G_T = G`. -/
theorem lemma_7_1 {n mA mB : ℕ} (G : CSG n mA mB) (T : Finset (Fin n)) :
    (∀ s, reachValue G T s = limAvgValue (targetGame G T) (targetReward T) s) ∧
    ((∀ s ∈ T, ∀ a b, (G.δ s a b).1 s = 1) → targetGame G T = G) := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
